From 1724ec22fa5403aa4bc46b7dce86699fb024c4c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 09:23:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 080/119] scene-referred S4: the .cube loader, and two LUTs the
 camera owns

The display chain needs two 3D LUTs - the creative look (LMT) and the output transform (ODT) -
and D8 puts both on the camera rather than in the renderer. The public IRenderer surface decides
the split: a plugin can create and refresh a 3D texture from CPU data (UploadToVideoMemory3D /
UpdateTextureInVideoMemory, the pair Cry3DEngine's SVO brick pools already use from outside the
renderer), but nothing in IRenderer can bind a texture to a pass or dispatch compute. So ccam
parses, converts and uploads; the renderer only samples.

- A Resolve-dialect .cube parser: comments, TITLE, LUT_3D_SIZE, optional DOMAIN_MIN/MAX, N^3
  triplets with the red index varying fastest. LUT_1D_SIZE, a missing size, a short grid and a
  non-unit domain are each refused with a message that says what is wrong; the shaper is analytic
  in the shader, so the file's domain is ACEScct [0,1] by construction and a cube on another
  domain is not a display transform for this chain.
- fp16 RGBA on the CPU before the upload: the upload path does not convert formats (source and
  destination must resolve to the same typeless DXGI format) and there is no three-channel fp16
  texture format. One mip, FT_NOMIPS | FT_DONT_STREAM | FT_STATE_CLAMP, repeat = false.
- Two slots, keyed on the requested path. On the common frame the work is one string compare; a
  path change reloads, a size change re-creates the texture rather than refreshing it in place,
  and a parse failure leaves the slot EMPTY rather than stale. Errors are logged once per path.
- Path resolution goes through ICryPak, first as given (relative to the project's asset
  directory) and then under %ENGINE%, so one string works in the editor and in the launcher
  whichever tree the Assets/ODT folder was installed into.
- Two new ccam property groups: "Look" (LMT File, empty = identity, D10) and "Output" (ODT File,
  default Assets/ODT/odt_srgb_100nit_aces2_65.cube). Plain reflected strings - a .cube is not a
  texture asset, so there is no resource picker to reuse.
- Four new post-effect bus params carry the result to the renderer: Global_User_LutODT / -Size
  and Global_User_LutLMT / -Size. Texture IDs travel as floats because the bus has no integer
  channel and an ID is far below the 2^24 a float represents exactly. Cached accessors on
  CPostEffectsMgr, like the scene-referred request and the pre-exposure beside them.

Nothing reads the LUTs yet: the tone map's output-transform branch is the next commit. Off the
switch not one line of this runs, and with the switch on but no consumer the picture is unchanged.

